lab (abalymani@alfaisal.edu).

This applies equally to the site's source code, stylesheet and content data
file. Making a repository public on GitHub grants only the rights described in
GitHub's Terms of Service — it does not place the work in the public domain
and does not grant an open-source licence.

================================================================================
3. WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT ASKING
================================================================================

  a. Read, link to, and share URLs of any page.
  b. Quote short passages for review, teaching, commentary or news reporting,
     with attribution to "CM-iTAD Lab, Alfaisal University" and a link.
  c. Cite the research. Where a figure appears in a published paper, cite the
     paper rather than this site. See /publications.html.
  d. Make the temporary copies a browser needs in order to display the site.

================================================================================
4. TEXT AND DATA MINING — RIGHTS EXPRESSLY RESERVED
================================================================================

The rightsholders expressly reserve all rights to carry out text and data
mining of this material, including for the training, fine-tuning, evaluation
or grounding of artificial-intelligence or machine-learning systems, and
including the compilation of this material into any corpus or dataset used for
those purposes.

This is a reservation of rights for the purposes of Article 4(3) of Directive
(EU) 2019/790 on copyright in the Digital Single Market, and an assertion of
the equivalent reservation available in other jurisdictions.

It is declared in machine-readable form in three places:

  - the `tdm-reservation` meta tag on every page of this site
  - the `noai, noimageai` robots directive on every page
  - /robots.txt, which names the harvesting agents this reservation applies to

Ignoring those declarations does not confer a licence.

Researchers who want to use this material for legitimate academic study are
welcome to ask — the lab's own work depends on that kind of access, and
permission is not usually withheld. Write to abalymani@alfaisal.edu.

